Subject: Cantor Phase3 Topology Scanner Justification

& [JustificationIdentity] is the M2 formation rationale
  + [justification_uuid] is 0e165d46-3154-4784-88cd-13ef2ead8e54
  + [status] is formation_justified_implementation_not_authorized

& [Problem] is lexical admission does not establish physical containment
  + [reparse] can redirect a descendant operation
  + [hard_link] can alias an outside regular file
  + [stream] can carry data outside ordinary filename inventory
  + [Git] controls can reinterpret repository boundaries
  + [race] can invalidate a previously observed tree

& [Solution] is a complete fail-closed topology receipt
  + [coverage] is the whole candidate because a workspace-root sandbox grants broad physical reach
  + [identity] uses the strongest generally available Windows file identity
  + [policy] initially rejects every indirection and unsupported case
  + [evidence] is deterministic, bounded, content-addressed, single-use, and explicitly non-atomic

& [WhyWin32] is an evidence requirement not a performance preference
  + [stable_Rust] exposes reparse attributes but not stable file identity, link count, or stream enumeration
  + [generated_binding] reduces ABI transcription risk
  + [isolation] limits the eventual unsafe surface to private read-only calls

& [WhyNotNeural] is proof semantics
  + [classification] must be exact for filesystem authority
  + [fault] must fail closed and reproduce
  + [model] may later explain a record but cannot substitute for OS identity evidence

& [WhyFormationOnly] is governance
  + [dependency] has not been reviewed or activated
  + [unsafe] has not been justified line by line
  + [fixtures] include security-sensitive alias creation
  + [sandbox] remains unproven for physical write boundaries

& [Rollback] is complete before integration
  + [formation] remove documents only
  + [M2A] remove pure forms and export
  + [M2C] remove scanner, Windows adapter, and target dependency
  + [state_migration] is none before M2E
